---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Photo from '../components/Photo.astro';
import Aurora from '../components/Aurora.astro';
import Scribble from '../components/Scribble.astro';
import { lensPhotos } from '../lib/photos';

const loves = ['People', 'Culture', 'Possibility', 'Dogs', 'Paneer butter masala', 'Harry Potter', 'Kindness', 'Food & sleep'];
const quote = 'In a world where you can be anything, be kind.';
const [lens1, lens2] = lensPhotos();
---
<Base title="Richa Saxena">
<main>

  <section class="hero">
    <Aurora />
    <div class="hero-text">
      <p class="hand hello">Hi, I'm</p>
      <h1 class="name" aria-label="Richa Saxena">
        <span class="w" aria-hidden="true"><span>Richa</span></span>{' '}
        <span class="w" aria-hidden="true"><span>Saxena</span></span>
      </h1>
      <p class="tagline">
        <span style="--i:0">Small-town heart.</span>
        <span style="--i:1">Strict-teacher energy.</span>
        <span style="--i:2">Soft spot for every dog I meet.</span>
      </p>
      <p class="hero-sub">
        People and culture leader, former teacher, co-founder of Uniify.
        I collect people's stories and turn them into <Scribble>kinder, happier workplaces</Scribble>.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Say hello <span aria-hidden="true">👋</span></a>
        <a href="#about" class="btn btn-ghost">Get to know me</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-photo">
      <div class="ring" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <Photo name="richa" alt="Richa Saxena smiling" label="Your photo here" class="portrait" priority widths={[400, 640, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 66vw, 400px" />
      <span class="sticker" style="--i:0; --rot:-6deg">🐾 dog person</span>
      <span class="sticker" style="--i:1; --rot:4deg">🍳 creates (or destroys) dishes</span>
      <span class="sticker" style="--i:2; --rot:-3deg">🎧 song on repeat</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="marquee" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="marquee-track">
      {[0, 1].map(() => loves.map(l => <><span>{l}</span><i>✦</i></>))}
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section about" id="about">
    <div class="about-main">
      <h2>A listener first.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        I was raised in Agra, a small town where neighbours look out for each other and
        helping someone is just what you do. I've lived in quite a few big cities since,
        but I still value <Scribble>people over polish</Scribble>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I love meeting different people and hearing their stories. Somewhere in those stories,
        I found a problem I knew I could solve. (More on that below.)
      </p>
      <p>
        Off the clock, I'm mom to a wonderful, awesome boy, a fiction lover
        (Harry Potter forever <button class="bolt" type="button" aria-label="A little magic">⚡</button>),
        and someone who truly believes the best things in life are <Scribble><strong>food and sleep</strong></Scribble>.
        Everything else is a bonus.
      </p>
    </div>

    <aside class="about-side">
      <div class="music-card glow" data-reveal="rise">
        <div class="eq" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
        <p class="music-line">While you're reading this, I'm probably listening to a song for the <strong>100th time</strong> today.</p>
        <p class="hand music-quote">"If music be the food of love, play on."</p>
      </div>

      <div class="twist-card" data-reveal="rise">
        <p class="twist-label">Plot twist</p>
        <h3>Don't go by the smile.</h3>
        <p>
          A colleague once showed our Christmas party photos to her family. Someone pointed at me and
          said, "Nobody could be scared of <em>her</em>." She laughed: "Don't go by that smile.
          The whole block is scared of her."
        </p>
        <p>
          Turns out, naughty kids were warned they'd be sent to my class. I could quiet any room,
          and was invited to train other teachers on how to do it too.
          <span class="smile" aria-hidden="true"><span>🙂</span><span>😈</span></span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="section beliefs">
    <h2>Three things I'd say in any room.</h2>
    <ul class="belief-list">
      <li data-reveal="rule" style="--i:0">
        <h3>People are more than they seem.</h3>
        <p>In good ways and not-so-good ways. That's exactly why kindness and empathy always help.</p>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal="rule" style="--i:1">
        <h3>Kindness doesn't check status.</h3>
        <p>
          My father spoke to everyone the same way, whoever they were: kindly. I grew up thinking that's simply
          how you talk to people. Everyone makes mistakes, they're human. So before I judge, I stand in their shoes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li data-reveal="rule" style="--i:2">
        <h3>Culture lives in small moments.</h3>
        <p>
          Not in celebrations, gifts and vouchers. In a peer's small gesture, a colleague's helping hand,
          a leader's fair decision, or someone standing by you when you need it most.
          The everyday things make a long journey together possible.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <blockquote class="big-quote" data-reveal="words">
      <p>"{quote.split(' ').map((w, i, all) => <><span style={`--i:${i}`}>{w}</span>{i < all.length - 1 && ' '}</>)}"</p>
      <footer class="hand">It's how I lead, and always will. Learned it from my dad. 💜</footer>
    </blockquote>
  </section>

  <section class="rooms">
    <h2 class="rooms-title">Different rooms, same person.</h2>
    <ul class="words">
      <li data-reveal="stamp"><span>Students called me</span> <strong>kind.</strong> <em>(even when I was strict)</em></li>
      <li data-reveal="stamp"><span>Teammates called me</span> <strong>reachable.</strong></li>
      <li data-reveal="stamp"><span>Clients called me</span> <strong>helpful.</strong></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section dogs" id="dogs">
    <div class="dogs-text">
      <h2>Every dog is <span class="nowrap">my dog. 🐾</span></h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Mine, strays, the neighbours'... I've loved too many to count. No dream breed, just doggos.
        <span class="aside">(Except the ones who don't love me back.)</span>
      </p>
      <p>Lately, my heart belongs to <strong>Thor</strong>, a beautiful German Shepherd next door.</p>
      <p class="hand big">One day, no dog near me will ever go hungry.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="polaroids" id="paw-zone">
      <figure class="polaroid p-main tilt" data-reveal="pin" style="--i:0">
        <Photo name="thor" as="div" alt="Thor, a German Shepherd" label="Thor 🐕" widths={[500, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 80vw, 440px" />
        <figcaption>Thor, my current favourite</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="polaroid p2 tilt" data-reveal="pin" style="--i:1">
        <Photo name="dog-1" as="div" alt="A dog I love" label="🐶" widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 40vw, 220px" />
        <figcaption>a good boy</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="polaroid p3 eaten tilt" data-reveal="pin" style="--i:2" aria-label="A joke photo frame with bite marks: a dog ate this image">
        <div class="pic chewed"><span>🐕<br>A dog ate<br>this image.</span></div>
        <figcaption>no regrets</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section kitchen" id="kitchen">
    <h2>I can create or destroy any dish.</h2>
    <p class="hand says">says my husband 🙃</p>

    <div class="recipe-grid">
      <article class="recipe tilt" data-reveal="deal" style="--i:0">
        <p class="r-tag">Signature</p>
        <h3>Paneer Butter Masala</h3>
        <p>The one everyone asks for. Mostly Indian at heart, always.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="recipe tilt" data-reveal="deal" style="--i:1">
        <p class="r-tag">Proudest moment</p>
        <h3>Eggs Benedict</h3>
        <p>The hollandaise came out gorgeous on the very first try. I was SO proud.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="recipe tilt" data-reveal="deal" style="--i:2">
        <p class="r-tag">Biggest adventure</p>
        <h3>Lockdown bread</h3>
        <p>The bread came out awesome. The microwave did not survive. 🫠</p>
      </article>
      <article class="recipe tilt" data-reveal="deal" style="--i:3">
        <p class="r-tag">Inspiration</p>
        <h3>MasterChef Australia</h3>
        <p>Watching it means trying their recipes. Trying their recipes means... see the title above.</p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="cooking glow halo" data-reveal="rise">
      <span class="pot" aria-hidden="true">🍳</span>
      <div>
        <h3>Something's cooking...</h3>
        <p>A new project where my love for food meets something bigger. Coming soon.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section journey" id="journey">
    <h2>From the classroom to the boardroom.<br><span class="hand accent">(same heart, bigger rooms)</span></h2>

    <div class="numbers">
      <div class="stat"><strong data-count="20" data-suffix="+">20+</strong><span>years developing people</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong data-count="2000" data-suffix="+">2,000+</strong><span>students taught</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><strong data-count="50" data-suffix="+">50+</strong><span>organisations advised</span></div>
    </div>

    <ol class="timeline">
      <li data-reveal="step">
        <span class="when">2003 - 2018</span>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="chip">🍎 The classroom</span>
          <h3>Educator, then Academic Coordinator &amp; Internal Auditor</h3>
          <p>
            15 years across six K-12 schools in Agra, Greater Noida and Chennai. I mentored a team of
            24 teachers, ran training workshops, welcomed new faculty, and kept quality high through audits.
          </p>
          <p class="highlight">
            2,000+ students later, some are in college now, and they still reach out to say <Scribble>I believed in them</Scribble>.
            That never gets old.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li data-reveal="step">
        <span class="when">2019 - now</span>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="chip">🚀 Uniify</span>
          <h3>Co-founder &amp; CHRO</h3>
          <p>
            I collected people's stories, and in them I found a problem worth solving: engagement, wellbeing
            and internal comms are deeply connected, yet most organisations manage them in silos.
            So we built Uniify to bring them together, so HR teams could see culture, act on it, and prove its impact.
          </p>
          <p>
            I owned the full employee journey for our own teams, from hiring and onboarding to engagement,
            performance and exits, while advising HR leaders at 50+ organisations across industries and countries.
          </p>
          <div class="story glow">
            <p class="story-title">Our first client came from 3,000 km away, in an industry we weren't sure about.</p>
            <p>
              Two wonderful women in Georgia took Uniify for a 2-month pilot. They worked in the casino space
              and doubted it would fit. One month in, they came back asking for a full subscription.
              Peer recognition went up 121% in a quarter.
            </p>
            <p class="hand">It worked where even we weren't sure it would. That's when we knew.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="award glow halo">
            <span class="trophy" aria-hidden="true">🏆</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Women in HR Tech, People's Choice Award 2024</h4>
              <p>For my contributions to HR tech through Uniify. Seeing my name next to so many wonderful women in this space? Awesome.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li data-reveal="step">
        <span class="when">2023 - now</span>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="chip">🤝 HRIN</span>
          <h3>Founding Member &amp; Community Admin</h3>
          <p>
            Helped shape HRIN, a closed, vetted global community for HR professionals, from its early days.
            Today I keep it a trusted space by vetting members and curating conversations.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li data-reveal="step">
        <span class="when">2025 - now</span>
        <div class="step">
          <span class="chip">⚖️ Chitkara University</span>
          <h3>Jury Member</h3>
          <p>
            I sit on startup screening and selection committees at the Chitkara Innovation Incubation Foundation
            for the MeitY GENESIS EiR Program and the Startup India Seed Fund Scheme.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="edu">
      <p class="hand">Studied biology, then English, then HR. Turns out people were always the subject.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>PGDBA, Human Resources</strong> Symbiosis Institute of Management Studies</li>
        <li><strong>M.A., English</strong> Dr. Bhim Rao Ambedkar University, Agra</li>
        <li><strong>B.Sc., Biology</strong> Dr. Bhim Rao Ambedkar University, Agra</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bring">
    <h2>The work I love doing.</h2>
    <ul class="bring-list">
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">🌱</span><h3>Culture building &amp; onboarding</h3><p>Values people actually live, and a first week people remember.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">🎉</span><h3>Engagement &amp; recognition</h3><p>Calendars, competitions and shout-outs that feel genuine.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">🧘</span><h3>Wellbeing strategy</h3><p>Mental health workshops, health check-ups, walkathons.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">👂</span><h3>Employee listening</h3><p>Surveys and polls that turn into action, not just reports.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">📣</span><h3>Internal &amp; leadership comms</h3><p>From Fun Fridays to town halls: before, during and after.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">📊</span><h3>People analytics &amp; HR tech</h3><p>Data that shows culture, so you can act on it and prove it.</p></li>
      <li><span class="ico" aria-hidden="true">🔎</span><h3>Talent acquisition</h3><p>Hiring for skills and for heart, with a real culture fit.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="section lens-teaser">
    <div class="lens-text">
      <h2>I click to keep memories alive.</h2>
      <p>Mostly nature. Always trying to capture the essence of something beautiful before it's gone.</p>
      <a href="/photos" class="btn btn-primary">See my photos <span aria-hidden="true">📸</span></a>
    </div>
    <a href="/photos" class="lens-pair" aria-label="See my photos">
      <Photo src={lens1} alt="" label="🌿" style="view-transition-name: lens-0" widths={[400, 700]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 50vw, 300px" />
      <Photo src={lens2} alt="" label="🌅" style="view-transition-name: lens-1" widths={[400, 700]} sizes="(max-width: 860px) 50vw, 300px" />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="hello-band">
    <h2>Want to say hello?</h2>
    <p>I read every message, usually with a song on repeat.</p>
    <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Write to me <span aria-hidden="true">✉️</span></a>
  </section>

</main>
</Base>
